  "text": "The air in the throne room did not merely grow cold; it crystallized, trapping the breath of every courtier in a sudden, suffocating stillness. King Aldric’s hand, which had hovered over the hilt of his sword, trembled not from fear, but from the sheer, crushing weight of the revelation. The High Priest’s words hung in the void, echoing louder than the roaring flames of the torches. To be erased from the future was a fate far worse than death; it was a negation of existence itself. Aldric looked down at his son, the infant who was no longer just a child, but a vessel for an ancient, hungry force. The silver veins on the boy’s back pulsed with a rhythm that defied biology, a syncopated beat that seemed to pull the very light from the room. The capital, once the proud heart of the empire, was now a ghost on the map, a memory fading into the expanding darkness. The king realized then that his dynasty had never been built on stone or steel, but on a fragile illusion of permanence that the boy’s birth had shattered. As the starry void in the infant’s eyes widened, Aldric felt his own identity begin to dissolve, his memories of conquest and glory turning to ash on his tongue. He was not a king anymore; he was a footnote in a story he could not read. The map on the boy’s back flared one last time, blindingly bright, and the silence that followed was not empty, but full of the terrifying promise of a world reborn in shadow."
}

